{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","type":"source","id":"SRC0854","tables":{"people":[],"organizations":[{"id":"ORG052","displayName":"Sirius-Verlag","authorizedName":"Sirius-Verlag","types":["publisher"],"city":["Vienna / Berlin"],"country":"Austria / Germany","slug":"sirius-verlag","contributionIds":["CON-S047-PUB-ORG052"],"workIds":["W-S047"],"sourceIds":["SRC0095","SRC0854","SRC0855"],"publicNote":"Music publishing house in Vienna and Berlin. It issued the Sirius-Mappen in six annual series from 1927 to January 1933, and from 1933 the successor publication Tonfilm Theater Tanz, which ran to 1943. No name register carries the firm: the GND holds three bodies called Sirius, one German, one unplaced and one an Austrian company registered under a legal form introduced in 2007, and none of them is this house.","authorizedNameSource":"local heading"}],"sources":[{"id":"SRC0854","shortCitation":"Sirius-Mappen (36 Hefte), Sirius-Verlag, Wien–Berlin, 1927–1933","fullCitation":"Sirius-Mappen (36 Hefte). Wien–Berlin: Sirius-Verlag, 1927–January 1933. Six annual series. Digitised set with an indexed list of 278 titles, Internet Archive. Accessed 27 August 2026.","title":"Sirius-Mappen (36 Hefte)","creator":"","publication":"Sirius-Mappen","repository":"Internet Archive","date":"1927–1933","accessDate":"2026-08-27","primaryUrl":"https://archive.org/details/sirius-mappe-3-12","sourceType":"sheet_music","reliability":"medium","sourceStatus":"verified","slug":"src0854-sirius-mappen-sirius-verlag-wien-berlin","researchNote":"The indexed contents name eight Kaper titles, each with its series and issue number: “Auf Wiederseh’n, Herr Doktor! Auf Wiederseh’n, Frau Doktor!” (4-05), “Sagen kleine Mädels ‘nein’” (5-07), “Mondnacht in Sanssouci” (6-02), “Heut’ bin ich gut aufgelegt!”, “Ich weiß ein kleines Café” and “Es wird schon wieder besser” (all 6-09), “Wer weint heut’ aus Liebe Tränen” (6-10) and “Tränen in der Geige” (7-01). All eight are lyrics by Fritz Rotter. The last carries a series n